studio — cheatsheet

The frame is the lens view, fm and the panel, laid out from the note
studio/frame (`design/lens`). A slot of tabs shows one at a time, its tab
line over it naming them, and the panel across the bottom holds the
terminals, each a tab. These are the frame's keys, in tmux and in gio's
window alike; ed's and fm's own are in their cheatsheets.

the keys
  Tab        in ed or a lens: the lens view's next tab, source, outline,
             render, diff, then the source again
  alt-t      t, the terminals: hide the panel, or show it again

the tab line — the names over a slot of tabs, each a button
  a name     show that tab
  +          a new terminal, on the panel's line
  ×          close the terminal shown, once there are two

A press sends what l would: l 2, l new, l close. In tmux the first five
names are buttons, and in gio's window every one.

l — the frame's verb, as vi's l steps right: the next tab (`sh/l`)
  l              the next tab of the slot it runs in
  l prev         the one before
  l 2            the tab at that place, from 1, as the tab line numbers it
  l outline      a tab by its name, from any pane of the frame
  l close        end the tab shown; the next takes its place, but a
                 slot keeps its last
  l new [cmd]    a terminal in the panel: a shell, or cmd
  studio tab     say the slot's tabs, * on the one shown
  studio panel   alt-t's verb: hide, show, or bare, turn

a lens — the outline, the render, the diff (studio show)
  j k          move, arrows too; the row moved to is said to cur, and
               ed's cursor goes to its line
  l h          the outline's part unfolded, and folded, as on the page:
               l on one unfolded goes in, h on one folded goes up and
               folds it
  enter        open what the row names; a right click does the same,
               and in the render opens the word it falls on
  t            the outline's rows, or its thumbs
  g G          the render's top and bottom, j k scrolling it
  q            outside a frame, quit; in one, q is fm's

No key types in a lens, so none changes the text out of sight.

what comes to the frame
  e file       said to cur, and the source tab shows, the eye on it
  spawn        a terminal in the panel, not a split; fm's a and ; too
  p -a         the word at the shell's prompt, as a middle click hands
               it, the panel shown first when hidden
  an exit      a terminal's: the next takes its place
